WEBVTT

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:06.100
This section is focused on a third
category of coping strategies.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:10.360
This category uses social support
to better cope with stress.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:14.180
The strategy is called
social support coping.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:18.796
Before we explain what we
mean by social support coping,

00:00:18.836 --> 00:00:22.260
we want to discuss one
aspect of having tinnitus.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.040
It is that tinnitus
is an invisible disability.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.830
That means that you
are dealing with an issue

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:31.840
or condition that a stranger cannot see.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.844
People who know that you have
tinnitus may understand when its

00:00:35.884 --> 00:00:39.068
symptoms are affecting you,
but a stranger will not be able

00:00:39.108 --> 00:00:42.740
to understand how you are being
affected by your tinnitus.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:47.580
Having an invisible disability may
affect many of your interactions.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:51.321
People may misinterpret some
of your behaviors or actions because

00:00:51.361 --> 00:00:56.020
they do not know or they forget
that you are dealing with tinnitus.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:01.120
Even besides the impact of your invisible
tinnitus, a lot of our stresses can come

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:05.780
from interpersonal interactions,
from misunderstandings and miscommunications.

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:09.319
This section will discuss
multiple issues about social

00:01:09.359 --> 00:01:13.020
support as a coping strategy
when you have tinnitus.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:18.234
In view that you have an invisible
disability, your decision to disclose

00:01:18.274 --> 00:01:22.290
the existence of your tinnitus is one
that you have to repeatedly make

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:27.500
as you interact with people in the community,
workplace and social arenas.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:30.703
You will have to decide
whom to tell and how much

00:01:30.743 --> 00:01:34.360
information to disclose about
your tinnitus-related issues.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:37.420
The amount of information you
want to disclose may differ

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:40.775
according to your social closeness
to the people in your personal,

00:01:40.815 --> 00:01:45.940
intimate or family life, in your work
or social life, and in the general public.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:51.200
Most likely, they will not be aware
of tinnitus issues unless you tell them.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.284
Sometimes you have to repeatedly tell them

00:01:53.324 --> 00:01:56.280
because tinnitus
is an invisible disability.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:00.447
Unless you give people a social cue,
they will not know or remember what

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:04.067
you are experiencing and why it might
be difficult for you to communicate

00:02:04.107 --> 00:02:08.100
freely with them or why you may
seem very distracted sometimes.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.720
They may attribute
your actions to something else.

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:13.878
So by stating that you have
tinnitus and by letting

00:02:13.918 --> 00:02:16.784
the person know how to better
communicate with you,

00:02:16.824 --> 00:02:22.240
you are taking some control and eliminating
some problems before they occur.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:25.860
We typically occupy a variety of different

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:29.240
positions in our connections
with other people.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:34.100
Think about the members of your personal
circle of friends and acquaintances.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:36.876
These members can be represented
by concentric circles,

00:02:36.916 --> 00:02:41.320
with the inner circle representing
your closest friends and family.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:44.804
If you are working, your outer
network may consist of acquaintances,

00:02:44.844 --> 00:02:46.360
friends and coworkers.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:50.610
We are pointing this out because you
may only feel comfortable sharing

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:54.780
information about your tinnitus
to the people in your inner circles.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:56.920
That is your choice.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.484
It is up to you to think
about your comfort zone

00:02:59.524 --> 00:03:02.880
as far as sharing information
about your tinnitus.

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:06.434
But keep in mind that if you
need some accommodations at work,

00:03:06.474 --> 00:03:11.288
even for small things like playing a radio
or a white noise machine in your office,

00:03:11.328 --> 00:03:15.120
you may have to disclose
your disability to your employer.

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:20.445
When you are working with or socializing
with people you do not know well,

00:03:20.485 --> 00:03:23.253
you can open a dialogue
that involves disclosure

00:03:23.293 --> 00:03:26.300
and negotiation about
your tinnitus symptoms.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:29.732
Make sure to describe a little
about how you experience

00:03:29.772 --> 00:03:34.580
your tinnitus symptoms because some
people may not know what it is.

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:39.700
And tinnitus symptoms are experienced
differently among different people.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:41.400
Here is an example.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:48.040
I have tinnitus and that means I have
a constant ringing in both of my ears.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:51.851
So when I try to talk with you
in a quiet office environment,

00:03:51.891 --> 00:03:54.900
I may get interference from my tinnitus.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:58.638
If we step into my office where
I have a white noise machine,

00:03:58.678 --> 00:04:02.340
I will actually be better
able to communicate with you.

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:06.680
Let us define the main
types of social support.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:12.760
This is support that people can ask
to receive as well as to give to others.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.487
Social support coping can involve help

00:04:15.527 --> 00:04:18.820
with either problem solving
or stress management.

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:21.429
Coping researchers differ on how many

00:04:21.469 --> 00:04:24.040
categories or types
of social support there are.

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:28.340
For our purposes, we can summarize this
debate about the number of categories

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:32.720
and say they can range from three
to five main types of social support.

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:35.438
Here are some of the common
categories of social

00:04:35.478 --> 00:04:38.280
support with a brief description of each.

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:40.820
Informational support.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:45.256
For example, information advice
or suggestions for dealing with questions

00:04:45.296 --> 00:04:49.800
that arise, such as health issues,
legal matters, and other life issues.

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:51.420
Tangible support.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:56.025
Money or other financial support, visiting
a friend to offer to help with repairs

00:04:56.065 --> 00:05:00.500
at home, or things like transportation,
assistance, or grocery shopping.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:02.840
Emotional support.

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:08.720
Words and actions that make a person feel
understood, cared about, and affirmed.

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:15.140
For example, emotional support may
include empathy, caring, love, or trust.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.320
Now to apply these categories to tinnitus.

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:24.058
Seeking or receiving informational
support refers to information,

00:05:24.098 --> 00:05:28.680
advice, or suggestions that you
may obtain about your tinnitus.

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:31.824
An example is information
about new sound machines

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:34.980
for tinnitus given
to you by an audiologist.

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:37.997
Tangible support means receiving money,

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:41.880
financial support, or other
help due to your tinnitus.

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:45.360
Examples include receiving financial
compensation due to tinnitus.

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:48.442
For instance, if tinnitus
occurred during military service,

00:05:48.482 --> 00:05:52.409
or job assistance from a rehabilitation
counselor who can help you

00:05:52.449 --> 00:05:56.580
determine accommodations for tinnitus
that you can use on the job.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:00.386
Emotional support refers
to the words and actions that you

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:04.900
receive which reflect caring
or understanding about your tinnitus.

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:08.695
An example is talking with someone
like a counselor or a friend

00:06:08.735 --> 00:06:12.260
about the effects of tinnitus
on your relationships.

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:17.000
Seeking social support is a great
strategy for dealing with stress.

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:22.502
Not everyone will like this concept because
most people like to live independently.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:27.829
You may be unwilling to ask for support
thinking, oh, I don't want to impose,

00:06:27.869 --> 00:06:32.762
or he should know me well enough to know
what I need, or what's the point,

00:06:32.802 --> 00:06:37.740
I won't get it anyway, or I've
always kept my problems to myself,

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:40.740
or I can figure this out by myself.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:45.647
Being strong and independent are good
qualities, yet there are times

00:06:45.687 --> 00:06:50.000
when we can learn new information
from communicating with others.
